class:: ChordStrength
summary:: Major/minor chord template strength
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks

description::
An original deterministic major/minor template matcher over supplied chroma, following the standard pitch-class/template approach surveyed by Gomez (2006). Each of 24 triads receives cosine similarity multiplied by a coverage factor: min(1, weakestChordTone/(0.05*totalChroma)). An explicit no-chord state has score threshold. Causal min-sum dynamic programming adds transitionPenalty when the state changes; exponential chroma smoothing is optional. Root is 0=C through 11=B; quality 0=major, 1=minor. Silence forces both indices to -1. Extended, suspended, inverted or incomplete chords can be ambiguous; this initial vocabulary deliberately contains only major/minor/no-chord.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chroma
A C-first Array of 12, 24, 36, or 120 nonnegative pitch-class values. Higher resolutions fold to nearest semitones where a twelve-class representation is required.

argument:: smooth
Causal exponential smoothing time in seconds, zero disables. Time follows the actual interval between trigger updates.

argument:: transitionPenalty
Nonnegative min-sum path cost for changing chord state. Higher values favour persistence; zero makes framewise choices.

argument:: threshold
Minimum similarity required to beat the no-chord state; default 0.65.

argument:: trig
A positive value processes this control block. For FFT-derived features pass chain >= 0 so each analysis frame is used once; default 1 processes each control block.

returns::
Selected chord similarity, or the best frame similarity when no chord is selected. This is not probability.

examples::
The analysis controls audible synthesis or processing. Boot the server first; use headphones or moderate speaker volume.
code::
(
Routine({
    var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2TonalExample = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(4096), source, 0.25);
        var chroma = HPCP.kr(chain, harmonics: 1);
        var strength = ChordStrength.kr(chroma, trig: chain >= 0);
        var sound = [source * 0.1, RLPF.ar(source, 200 + (strength * 5000), 0.3) * 0.2];
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;
    ~mir2TonalBuffer = buffer;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::

Stop and release:
code::
(
~mir2TonalExample.free;
~mir2TonalBuffer.free;
)
::

